      "challenges": [
        "1,991 alerts; 1,991 verified (100.0%), 256 validated suspects, 256 investigated (100.0%), and 112 transferred. Six provinces have numeric alert rows (Haut-Uele, Bas-Uele, Ituri, Nord-Kivu, Sud-Ubangi and Tshopo); Sud-Kivu is unavailable, not zero.",
        "Nord-Kivu prints 382 hospitalised patients, including 263 in normed structures, and 63.0% occupancy without a bed count. The rate matches neither 263/354 (74.3%) nor 382/354 (107.9%) against the last printed 354 beds (SR135), and repeats prior editions. It is withheld as a conflict; 119 patients are outside normed structures.",
        "Contact follow-up 24,673/30,973 (79.7%). The six province rows sum exactly to the national 24,673/30,973. Nord-Kivu prints 76.8%, but its own 10,560/13,790 is 76.6%; the computed rate is used and the printed rate preserved. Sud-Kivu is unavailable, not zero. The national rate moved from 73.8% the day before (the unpublished 3 October edition; the last published edition printed 73.1%), and no province followed all of its contacts.",
        "PoE/PoC Table 4 reports three alerts, all in Ituri: two at the DGRPI Nizi PoC were isolated and invalidated after secondary screening, and one at the Mabakese PoC (Mambasa) was validated, investigated and transferred (1/1). Screening at the Zunguluka PoC (Mambasa) has been interrupted since 3 October after an attack attributed to ADF/NALU, and the Butuhe PoC (Nord-Kivu) has not operated since the 26 September security incident.",
        "Ituri ring opening is 20/32 (62.5%). In Nord-Kivu, ring opening is 12/25 (48.0%), household decontamination 14/40 (35.0%) and the mean infection-prevention score of assessed facilities 33%."
